# ---- Unity generated ----
[Ll]ibrary/
[Tt]emp/
[Oo]bj/
# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. Unity's stock .gitignore leaves these
# unanchored, which would also swallow Studio/build/ — the dotnet projects and
# gate scripts that let CI verify Core without a Unity licence.
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
[Ll]ogs/
[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
[Mm]emoryCaptures/
[Rr]ecordings/

# Asset meta data for files that no longer exist
!/[Aa]ssets/**/*.meta

# Unity3D generated
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta
sysinfo.txt
*.unitypackage
*.app
crashlytics-build.properties

# ---- IDE / solution files ----
# Only ignore Unity-generated project files at the repo root.
# The hand-written dotnet projects under Studio/build/ MUST stay tracked,
# because they are what lets CI run the Core tests without a Unity license.
/*.csproj
/*.sln
/*.unityproj
/*.sln.DotSettings.user
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.userprefs

# ---- dotnet build output ----
Studio/build/**/bin/
Studio/build/**/obj/
Studio/build/**/TestResults/
Studio/sim/**/bin/
Studio/sim/**/obj/

# Simulation metrics are regenerated on every run; the durable record of a run is
# the evidence file under Studio/evidence, not this scratch output.
Studio/evidence/sims/metrics.json
# Same category: the pre/post comparison pair a T3 criterion asks for. The
# durable record is the evidence file, which carries the verdict and every
# metric value inline -- see EVD-0007. Tracking the raw pair also breaks
# EveryKernelDocumentIsCoveredByTheManifest, since they are sim output rather
# than kernel documents and no schema governs them.
Studio/evidence/sims/metrics_*.json

# JARVIS renders the studio's own state into one page. The page is derived from
# the records under Studio/, so committing it would create a second copy that
# goes stale the moment anything is filed -- and a stale cockpit is worse than
# no cockpit. Regenerate with: python3 Studio/jarvis/build-jarvis.py
Studio/jarvis/jarvis.html

# ---- OS ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
